      "In 1687, Isaac Newton published three laws that describe how objects move. First, some terms.",
      "A force is a push or a pull on an object. Force is measured in newtons (N). Mass is the amount of matter in an object, measured in kilograms (kg); it is not the same as weight, which is the force of gravity pulling on that mass. Velocity is speed in a particular direction. Acceleration is any change in velocity: speeding up, slowing down, or changing direction. It is measured in metres per second squared (m/s²). The net force is the total of all forces on an object once they are combined; balanced forces cancel out to a net force of zero.",
