      "Worked example: you push a 50 kg shopping cart with a net force of 100 N. Rearranging F = ma gives a = F ÷ m = 100 ÷ 50 = 2 m/s². Load the cart to 100 kg and the same push gives only 1 m/s².",
      "Newton's third law: for every action force there is an equal and opposite reaction force. Forces always come in pairs acting on two different objects. When you push on a wall, the wall pushes back on you with the same strength. A rocket pushes hot gas downward out of its engines, and the gas pushes the rocket upward. When you walk, your foot pushes backward on the ground and the ground pushes you forward.",
