      "Everything around you is made of atoms, tiny particles far too small to see with an ordinary microscope. An element is a pure substance made of only one kind of atom, such as gold, oxygen, or carbon.",
      "Atoms are made of three smaller particles:\n- Protons have a positive electric charge and sit in the nucleus, the dense centre of the atom.\n- Neutrons have no charge (they are neutral) and also sit in the nucleus.\n- Electrons have a negative charge, are far lighter, and move in the space around the nucleus.",
